  "comparisonProfiles": [
    {
      "id": "semantic-pptx-mutate-v1",
      "description": "PPTX presentations compared as an ORDERED list of slides (slide order is part of the model — `move-slide` is the whole point of this vocabulary), each an ORDERED list of shapes, each shape's kind/text/position. Both producers' projections are re-derived from raw OPC/XML bytes by the SAME independent `zip`+`quick-xml` reader (never trusted from either producer's own typed model), scoped to exactly what `crate::artifacts::pptx::schema::snapshot::PptxShape` itself models: shape kind (textBox/placeholder/picture/other), a placeholder's own `phKind`, a shape's text content (paragraph boundaries joined by newline — per-run bold/italic/font-size styling is writer freedom, not normative here), and its `a:xfrm` position in EMUs (a shape with no explicit `a:xfrm`, inheriting its position from the slide layout, projects as x=y=cx=cy=0 on both sides — the same default `crate::artifacts::pptx`'s own importer uses for a missing `a:xfrm`). OPC-level plumbing a rebuilt slide mints fresh on every call — slide/shape XML part paths, relationship ids, `p:sldId`'s numeric `id`, `p:cNvPr`'s shape id/name, which slideLayout a rebuilt slide targets — is deliberately absent from the projection because `PptxSnapshot`'s own typed model does not track it either; it is OPC packaging freedom, not shape content.",
      "arrays": "ordered",
      "ignoreKeys": []
    }
  ],
